'' A refused format string in Format is a bug in the program: the reason and the offset go to
'' stderr, then run-time error 1 stops it. Nothing after the call runs. Not a literal, which
'' the compiler would refuse first (TKO0851).
#import "std/strings"
dim as ustring f = "x={} y={} z={}"
print "before"
print strings.Format( f, 1, 2 )
print "not reached"
